# Node
node_modules/
*.log

# Host-package staging output (build:hosts → dist/{claude-code,codex}); regenerated,
# never committed. Anchored to repo root so it does NOT match the tracked hooks/dist/
# or mcp-servers/*/dist build artifacts. (universal-host-p0 L2; FU-3 resolved.)
/dist/

# Committed verification receipts (verified-multi-host-support L0 §6.1/§7.5 +
# desktop-app smoke receipts). The evidence store is SHARED-SCRUBBED and tracked,
# but NARROWLY: only the receipt trees under evidence/host-smoke/** and
# evidence/desktop-app-smoke/** are admitted. Everything else under evidence/ stays
# ignored so a stray operator artifact placed ADJACENT can never be committed
# (SEC-m1). These allow-lists are DISJOINT from /dist/ above (packages are
# regenerated, never tracked) so the two audit scans (`.guild/runs` share-set vs
# the package/receipt path-anchored scan) neither overlap nor gap. The audit.ts
# §7.2 scan is anchored to the same receipt trees.
/evidence/**
!/evidence/host-smoke/
!/evidence/host-smoke/**
!/evidence/desktop-app-smoke/
!/evidence/desktop-app-smoke/**

# Anchor to repo root: `!.guild/` (unanchored, no internal /) would re-include nested
# dirs like hooks/.guild/ or scripts/.guild/. Leading / anchors to gitignore directory.
# .guild/ — share-dot-guild policy (see docs/knowledge/decisions/guild-boundary-config-and-tracking.md Decision E)
.guild
!/.guild/
# HIGH (share-dot-guild risk-gate remediation, Decision J): default-deny every
# top-level entry directly inside .guild/ so an unlisted/new subtree (e.g. a
# future .guild/<new-thing>/) is NEVER silently committable by default — mirrors
# the /evidence/** allow-list pattern above (deny-all, then narrowly re-include).
# Each subtree below must be explicitly re-included: directories need the
# two-line `!.guild/<dir>/` + `!.guild/<dir>/**` shape (the first line un-ignores
# the directory itself so git will recurse into it at all; the second re-includes
# its contents — gitignore will not check per-file rules inside a still-ignored
# parent directory). A file-only re-include is a single `!.guild/<file>` line.
# Anything NOT named below stays ignored — this is the fix for the audit finding
# that .guild/context/, .guild/diagnose/, .guild/index.sqlite, etc. were
# committable-by-default with no re-include line at all.
.guild/*
!.guild/guild.yaml
!.guild/adoption-manifest.json
!.guild/agents/
!.guild/agents/**
!.guild/skills/
!.guild/skills/**
!.guild/workflows/
!.guild/workflows/**
!.guild/loops/
!.guild/loops/**
!.guild/wiki/
!.guild/wiki/**
!.guild/knowledge/
!.guild/knowledge/**
!.guild/memory/
!.guild/memory/**
!.guild/initiatives/
!.guild/initiatives/**
!.guild/init/
!.guild/init/**
!.guild/spec/
!.guild/spec/**
!.guild/plan/
!.guild/plan/**
!.guild/prd/
!.guild/prd/**
!.guild/team/
!.guild/team/**
!.guild/teams/
!.guild/teams/**
!.guild/artifacts/
!.guild/artifacts/**
!.guild/reflections/
!.guild/reflections/**
!.guild/evolve/
!.guild/evolve/**
!.guild/indexes/
!.guild/indexes/**
!.guild/workspace/
!.guild/workspace/**
!.guild/workspace-knowledge/
!.guild/workspace-knowledge/**
!.guild/workspace.json
!.guild/settings.json
!.guild/runs/
!.guild/runs/*/
# Re-deny everything inside runs/<id>/ — FU-C: tighten to named-files-only.
# Previously un-ignoring runs/<id>/ as a dir let any file through (run-state.json,
# ad-hoc receipts). Now only the named handoffs/+files/dirs below are shared.
# run-state.json IS in the FU-C re-include set: scripts/lib/shared/share-set.ts
# already declares it shareable (canonical intent) — the ONE pre-existing tracked
# instance (.guild/runs/run-809080ff-.../run-state.json) was untracked separately
# below because it predates scrub verification; future instances are committable
# post-scrub via this re-include.
.guild/runs/*/**
!.guild/runs/*/handoffs/
!.guild/runs/*/handoffs/**
!.guild/runs/*/verify.md
!.guild/runs/*/review.md
!.guild/runs/*/provenance.json
!.guild/runs/*/run.yaml
!.guild/runs/*/summary.md
!.guild/runs/*/share-payloads.flag
!.guild/runs/*/run-state.json
!.guild/runs/_archive/rename-manifest.yaml
!.guild/runs/_archive/rename-runs.mjs

# Re-deny operator-private / local-only sub-paths (D-SHR-4 + Decision G), plus
# derived/runtime artifacts named explicitly for the audit trail even though the
# `.guild/*` default-deny above already covers unlisted entries.
# `.guild/runs/current-run-id` is a bare FILE directly under runs/ — NOT covered
# by the `!.guild/runs/*/` (directories-only, one level) re-include, so it needs
# its own explicit deny.
.guild/settings.local.json
.guild/hosts/
.guild/index.sqlite
.guild/runs/current-run-id
.guild/indexes/model-catalog/

# Fixture .guild/ dirs must be tracked (they are static test fixtures, not live runtime state).
# These exemptions are non-negotiable — preserved verbatim per share-dot-guild constraints.
# Keep this list in sync with FIXTURE_EXEMPT_PATTERNS in plugin/scripts/dot-guild/audit.ts (FU-F).
# MUST come after the bare (unanchored) `.guild` blanket-ignore rule above — gitignore
# resolves overlapping patterns by file order, so a fixture exemption declared BEFORE
# that blanket rule is silently re-excluded by it. (Previously misplaced above the
# blanket rule: the exemption was vacuous for any newly-added fixture file — only
# looked correct because the existing fixture files were already tracked, and git
# never re-applies ignore rules to already-tracked paths. Discovered while adding new
# guild-memory/guild-telemetry MCP fixtures; see mcp-servers/**/fixtures*/.guild/**.)
!benchmark/fixtures/**/.guild/
!benchmark/fixtures/**/.guild/**
!mcp-servers/guild-memory/fixtures/**/.guild/
!mcp-servers/guild-memory/fixtures/**/.guild/**
!mcp-servers/guild-telemetry/fixtures/**/.guild/
!mcp-servers/guild-telemetry/fixtures/**/.guild/**
!mcp-servers/guild-telemetry/fixtures-v14/**/.guild/
!mcp-servers/guild-telemetry/fixtures-v14/**/.guild/**
!mcp-servers/guild-telemetry/fixtures-alt-cwd/**/.guild/
!mcp-servers/guild-telemetry/fixtures-alt-cwd/**/.guild/**
!tests/dot-guild/fixtures/**/.guild/
!tests/dot-guild/fixtures/**/.guild/**
# tests/wiki-lint/fixtures/**/.guild/ was declared EXEMPT in FIXTURE_EXEMPT_PATTERNS
# (plugin/scripts/dot-guild/audit.ts) but had NO matching re-include here — a real
# drift between the two allow-lists this audit pass found via the exemption-parity
# test (scripts/dot-guild/__tests__/exemption-parity.test.ts). Latent/harmless only
# because no wiki-lint fixture has ever needed a nested .guild/ yet; fixed here so
# the exemption and the re-include stay in lockstep.
!tests/wiki-lint/fixtures/**/.guild/
!tests/wiki-lint/fixtures/**/.guild/**
!hooks/__tests__/fixtures/golden-full-learn-run/.guild/
!hooks/__tests__/fixtures/golden-full-learn-run/.guild/**

# Point-in-time SC-11 remediation (Decision J risk-gate, this audit pass): these
# plugin-specific paths were found tracked-in-error (leaked past the pre-fix
# allow-list, before the `.guild/*` default-deny above existed). They are
# already covered by the default-deny (unlisted subtrees) but are named here as
# an explicit incident record. Kept BELOW the fixture-exemption block so the
# canonical share-dot-guild block above stays byte-identical across the 4
# workspace repos (tests/dot-guild/gitignore-equivalence.test.ts).
.guild/context/run-host-adapter-reconcile-20260621/
.guild/diagnose/20260626T101814Z-evolve-run-left-open.md

# Re-deny the model-catalog discovery cache: a LOCAL-ONLY, rebuildable, derived
# artifact (guild.model_catalog.v1 target-scoped cache) — never committed/exported/
# shared. This later rule wins over the !.guild/indexes/** re-include above.
.guild/indexes/model-catalog/
# Re-deny the structural-cache sidecar: a LOCAL-ONLY, rebuildable, derived artifact (our deterministic extractor output) — never committed/exported/shared. This later rule wins over the !.guild/indexes/** re-include above, so even where .guild/indexes/** is tracked a tampered cache can never be committed (FIX-T4.1-r6; threat model in scripts/understand/lib/bundle-validate.ts).
**/*.structural-cache.json

# .claude/ — Claude Code config (FU-D: dev-team agents + settings.json default
# to tracked when explicitly added; settings.local.json holds the operator's
# permission allowlist and stays local). Content commit (`git add .claude/...`)
# is a separate operator action — agents/ has drifted across workspace + plugin
# and wants reconciliation first.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Nested .guild/ enforcement: ONE .guild/ per project (git repo) root.
# The runtime resolver `plugin/hooks/lib/guild-root.ts` walks up to the
# nearest .git/.guild/ so hooks never create nested .guild/. The static
# check is `plugin/scripts/dot-guild/audit.ts` (FU-F) — CI fails on any
# non-fixture nested .guild/. No gitignore safety net is needed.

# Host-tool builtin-skill symlinks (operator-machine-specific; e.g. AionUI
# builtins symlinked into ~/.aionui-config). Not Guild's multi-host adapter
# layout — never part of the shipped plugin.
.codex/skills/
.gemini/skills/
.claude/skills/

